mirror-then-turn (MT) seen line: "Trefoil: mirror +3"
  reveal: Turning the mirrored trefoil over left every mark plus: turning over is a way of moving it, so its hand stayed right. Mirroring turned every mark plus, and no wiggling gets back: the trefoil is not its own mirror image, as Max Dehn proved in 1914. | The figure-eight is different: it is its own mirror image. So a trefoil comes in a left and a right version, and turning one over never swaps them.

turn-then-mirror (TM) seen line: "Trefoil: turned over −3 · mirror +3"
  reveal: Turning the trefoil over left every mark minus: turning over is a way of moving it, so its hand stayed left. Mirroring turned every mark plus, and no wiggling gets back: the trefoil is not its own mirror image, as Max Dehn proved in 1914. | The figure-eight is different: it is its own mirror image. So a trefoil comes in a left and a right version, and turning one over never swaps them.

